# Max/MSP OSC Controlee

**Type:** OSC Controlee
**Category:** Audio/Visual Programming
**Status:** Active
**Last Updated:** 2025-12-14

## Overview

Max/MSP is a visual programming language for music and multimedia. It provides OSC support for interactive audio/visual applications, live performance, and media control systems.

## OSC Integration

### Native Support
- **Full native OSC support** via udpreceive/send objects
- **Port:** 4000 (default)
- **Protocol:** OSC 1.0
- **Object-based:** OSC routing through Max objects

### Setup
- Add `udpreceive 4000` object to receive OSC
- Add `udpsend` objects to send OSC
- Route messages to desired parts of patch

## Available Operations

### Message Types
- `send_bang` - Send bang messages to receivers
- `send_float` - Send float values to receivers
- `toggle_dsp` - Toggle audio processing on/off

## Usage Examples

### Bang Messages
```
maxmsp_manager("send_bang", receiver="play")        # Trigger play button
maxmsp_manager("send_bang", receiver="stop")        # Trigger stop button
maxmsp_manager("send_bang", receiver="record")      # Start recording
```

### Float Values
```
maxmsp_manager("send_float", receiver="volume", value=0.8)    # Set volume to 80%
maxmsp_manager("send_float", receiver="frequency", value=440.0) # Set frequency
maxmsp_manager("send_float", receiver="pan", value=0.0)      # Center pan
```

### DSP Control
```
maxmsp_manager("toggle_dsp")  # Toggle audio on/off
```

## Receiver System

### Common Receivers
- **Transport:** play, stop, record, pause
- **Parameters:** volume, pan, frequency, resonance
- **Effects:** delay_time, feedback, reverb_mix
- **Visual:** opacity, position_x, position_y
- **Custom:** User-defined receiver names

### Message Routing
- Receivers connect to various Max objects
- Route to audio effects, visual elements, control logic
- Enable complex interactive systems

## Integration Patterns

### Live Performance
- Real-time parameter control
- Interactive music systems
- Live coding environments
- Performance control interfaces

### Interactive Installations
- Sensor-driven audio/visual responses
- Audience interaction systems
- Environmental control systems
- Multi-modal experiences

### Media Control
- Automated playback systems
- Interactive video installations
- Sound design control interfaces
- Real-time mixing consoles

## Technical Notes

### OSC Addresses
- Format: `/{receiver_name}`
- Examples: `/volume`, `/play`, `/frequency`
- Receivers defined in Max patch

### Message Types
- **Bang:** Trigger events, no data
- **Float:** Numeric values, automatic routing
- **DSP Toggle:** Audio engine control

### Timing
- Real-time capable (< 5ms latency)
- Suitable for live performance
- Synchronized with audio engine

## Common Workflows

### Performance Control
```
# Real-time performance control
maxmsp_manager("send_float", receiver="master_volume", value=0.9)
maxmsp_manager("send_bang", receiver="scene_change")
maxmsp_manager("send_float", receiver="effect_intensity", value=0.7)
```

### Interactive Systems
```
# Sensor integration
maxmsp_manager("send_float", receiver="light_level", value=sensor_reading)
maxmsp_manager("send_bang", receiver="motion_detected")
```

